    <string name="legends_title">Legends of Venezuela</string>
    <string name="rules_caida">Played with a 40-card Spanish deck and a race to 24 points. You get 3 cards and 4 are placed on the table. If you hold a card with the same number as the last one on the table, slap it: that is a caída. You can also call ronda, trivilín, patrulla, vigía, registro, maguaro, registríco, casa chica or casa grande. When the deck runs out, each extra card adds points. First to 24 wins!</string>
    <string name="rules_ludo">Each player has 4 tokens in their base. You need a 6 to leave the base and you roll again after a 6. If you land on a rival token outside the safe squares, it goes back to its base. Travel around the board and enter your color lane; reach the center with all 4 tokens to win.</string>
    <string name="rules_fiesta">Each player gets 7 cards. Play a card matching the color or number of the center card. Action cards skip, reverse or make others draw. Wilds change the color; +4 makes the next player draw four. When you have one card left, shout Fiesta! First to empty their hand wins.</string>
    <string name="rules_kemix">All cards are shuffled face down. On your turn flip two cards. If they are the same family, you keep the pair and play again; if not, they turn back. The player with the most pairs when every card is matched wins.</string>
    <string name="rules_nervioso">Take turns discarding a card and saying a number out loud (1, 2, 3…). If the number matches the card, everyone must slap the pile: the last one takes all the cards. If you slap with no match, you take the pile too. First to run out of cards wins.</string>
